# Copy to .env and put your real key in it. .env is gitignored and is the
# only file in this tree that holds the key.
#
# The key is NOT a build input. `make run` reads this file inside the recipe's
# shell, writes the value to a mode-0600 temp file in $TMPDIR (outside the
# repository), passes it to QEMU as
#
#     -fw_cfg name=opt/fableos/apikey,file=<that temp file>
#
# and deletes the temp file however the run ends. The kernel reads the blob at
# boot (drivers/fwcfg/) into RAM, strips the trailing newline this file will
# have, and reports only how many bytes arrived — never the key itself.
#
# With no key the kernel boots exactly the same, says it has none, and the API
# answers 401. That is the default developer experience and what the tests
# assume.
#
# $ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is used when this file has no key, so `export
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...` also works and leaves nothing on disk at all.
KEY="sk-ant-..."
